    "result_text": "Done. Tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2).\n\nI agree with the finding and applied it. `Soundex` is a pure, domain-agnostic standard string algorithm \u2014 a sibling of `Luhn` and `Hashes`, both of which the codebase keeps in `function/common` (and `Luhn` too has only owner-domain consumers), so \"single consumer is in owner\" was the wrong reason for its placement.\n\nChanges:\n- Moved `Soundex` to `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.common`.\n- Made it `public` (like `Luhn`/`Hashes`) and dropped the \"kept out of the function classes / one public method\" javadoc note, which only applies to the owner-package helpers neighboring function classes \u2014 matching how `Luhn`/`Hashes` omit it. Reworded the class javadoc to the `common` style (leads with what it computes and why, plus the \"pinned so both arms agree\" note).\n- Added `import ...common.Soundex` in `IdentityKey` (right next to its existing `Hashes` import) and in `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`; the `{@link Soundex}` references now resolve through those imports.\n\nNo logic or acceptance behaviour changed \u2014 the algorithm is byte-for-byte identical, just relocated.",
